    "done_when": "(1) Attribution: run the three tests on the H200, one job per revision through RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 scripts/nova_lane/run.sh (H200 rung, betelgeuse gpu_0003_grpA, one card, explicit --mem, JAX_PLATFORMS=cuda, the shared interpreter, no uv on the compute node; the coordinator authorises this launch path, and the general srun/sbatch/salloc fence does not forbid it), each from a detached scratch checkout under /tmp (git worktree add --detach, the shared .venv symlinked in, removed afterwards without --force), at exactly these revisions: the parent and the merge of the frozen-Newton lineage (db580bec8^1, db580bec8), the parent and the merge of the clip-mode request field (af7403bc0^1, af7403bc0), and main e53e1141d. Commit one log per revision under docs/figures/forward-solver-route-integrity/derivative-tests-root-cause/ with a table of revision, test and measured value. (2) Mechanism: for each test that changes between a parent and its merge, name the function and computation responsible from that diff, measured, not inferred (for example whether the derivative now passes through the frozen partition, the live fallback program or a stop_gradient, and what the custom derivative rule does at the terminal state). For a test that fails at every revision, say so and report what it compares and how far it is from passing. Fix nothing; the fix is a separate node. Write the findings into docs/evidence/fragments/forward-solver-route-integrity/fsri-derivative-tests-root-cause.html. While jobs run write status: blocked with wait_probe [\"sacct\",\"-n\",\"-X\",\"-j\",\"<comma-separated ids>\",\"--format=State\"] and wait_terminal COMPLETED. Every uv command carries --no-sync and nothing runs uv sync. The manifest status is one of complete, blocked or failed.",
